  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Ddd01025617 may be a target of Thrombopoietin through multiple indirect pathways. The first path links Ddd01025617 to Pigment epithelium-derived factor, which in turn is targeted by a complex molecule that ultimately leads to Thrombopoietin. The second path connects Ddd01025617 to Natural resistance-associated macrophage protein 2, which is targeted by Npc133119, which also targets Thrombopoietin. The third path links Ddd01025617 to Integrin beta-7, which is targeted by a compound that ultimately targets Thrombopoietin. These pathways collectively suggest that Ddd01025617 may be a downstream target of Thrombopoietin through various molecular intermediates. The evidence supports a potential regulatory relationship where Thrombopoietin influences the activity of these proteins, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear.",
